# Brenz Data

Source: `@docs/architecture/brenz-architecture-data.md`.

## Rules
- Use the path `users/{uid}` with subcollections `classLogs` and `waterLogs`.
- Store one document per class and one document per glass, with `registeredAt` as the device `Date`.
- Create one DTO per document with `Codable`, `toEntity()` and `init(entity)`.
- Read `@DocumentID var id: String?`. Throw an error in `toEntity()` if the `id` is nil.
- Generate the id on create with `document().documentID`.
- Store enums as `String`. Convert with the `.unknown` fallback in `toEntity()`.
- Calculate the local day on the device with `Calendar`.
- Write optimistically: return without waiting for the server on classes and water.
- `SignUp`, `SignIn`, `ResetPassword`, `ChangePassword` and `DeleteAccount` wait for the server up to ~10 s. After that they show "no network" and complete nothing.
- Translate Firebase errors to `AuthError` and `DataError`. Log with `os.Logger`.
- Sign out in this order: wait for writes (3 s), sign out of Auth, clear the Firestore cache, delete the user's `UserDefaults`, cancel reminders, rebuild repositories. `hasLaunchedBefore` is not deleted. It is not user data.
- Delete the account in this order: reauthenticate, delete Firestore data in batches, delete the Auth user, clean local data. `hasLaunchedBefore` is not deleted. It is not user data.
- Read Remote Config in the background. Interval 12 h in production, 0 in debug. Validate each value and use the default if it is out of range.
- Store `MessageRotationStore` in `UserDefaults`, per user.
- Schedule one weekly reminder per chosen day. Request permission only when it is turned on. Reconcile on app open.
- Keep the Firestore rules in `firebase/` with emulator tests.

## Forbidden
- Do not use `@ServerTimestamp` in `registeredAt`.
- Do not invent a `UUID` when the `id` is missing.
- Do not store message rotation in Firestore.
- Do not allow editing `registeredAt` or `elementId` of a class in the rules.
- Do not expose Firebase types outside `Data/Firebase/`.
- Do not add Analytics or Crashlytics.
- Do not raise `min_version` before Apple approves that version.
